  bx('gr', '<b>PYQs:</b> <b>2012 (C)</b> cooler aloft because air is heated from the ground up + thinner air; NOT more moisture. <b>2012 (D)</b> CO₂ absorbs <b>infrared</b>: transparent to incoming, opaque to outgoing radiation. <b>2023 (C)</b> water vapour absorbs infrared (also: equator insolation 10× poles ✘; IR two-thirds of insolation ✘; IR not visible spectrum ✘). <b>2024 (a)</b> troposphere thicker at equator because strong convection lifts heat. <b>2024 (d)</b> atmosphere heated more by terrestrial (long-wave) than incoming radiation; only Statement II right. <b>Undated (d, II and III)</b>: without atmosphere nights freeze but days get extremely hot, so “below freezing everywhere” ✘. <b>Mains 2022 (15m)</b> troposphere: clouds, air masses, jet streams sit here; terrestrial radiation is prime heat source.'),
